                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shuffling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "070b3122-4b42-3831-bdc6-0a74c7d12791",
                                        "entry_id": "cb35dc27-32d9-3432-9f79-271221b42bf8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act or motion of one who shuffles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "660b0714-a25c-41c7-931b-2e30b0956b6b",
                                                "sense_id": "070b3122-4b42-3831-bdc6-0a74c7d12791",
                                                "text": "Jane Gibson taught the cast the movements of the various creatures they were representing: the linear shufflings of the hedgehogs, the dozy lollopings of the rabbits, the sinuous dartings of the weasel and so on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ab048d0b-3098-3a86-846a-7735b7e7cd23",
                                        "entry_id": "cb35dc27-32d9-3432-9f79-271221b42bf8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The noise created by something moving about."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9eb416d3-52f8-4acd-b1e1-311becf88433",
                                                "sense_id": "ab048d0b-3098-3a86-846a-7735b7e7cd23",
                                                "text": "He would also have been exposed to the coughings and shufflings, comings and goings, questions and answers, wailings and slammings, snivellings and sneezings, etc., which figured so prominently in the reference room […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bf7b3f1c-e617-386f-b421-278ff82ccf26",
                                        "entry_id": "cb35dc27-32d9-3432-9f79-271221b42bf8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Trickery."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eb8afc2-623e-400a-8a90-5497c554244e",
                                                "sense_id": "bf7b3f1c-e617-386f-b421-278ff82ccf26",
                                                "text": "Then he warmed to it, and smoothly set out all his shifts, malices, and treacheries, his extreme boldnesses (he was desperate bold); his retreats, shufflings, and counterfeitings (he was also inconceivably a coward) […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shuffling",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ef5c434-805e-3cdd-bea1-8e9aadc0b3a3",
                                        "entry_id": "5272bd66-4104-336c-8bf5-0a6533d73de8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Moving with a dragging, scraping step."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01257d33-2af7-40d1-a433-5682e90ef0b1",
                                                "sense_id": "3ef5c434-805e-3cdd-bea1-8e9aadc0b3a3",
                                                "text": "This world I do renounce, and in your sights / Shake patiently my great affliction off."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72dc7b95-6990-3481-a3ea-2841df1f760a",
                                        "entry_id": "5272bd66-4104-336c-8bf5-0a6533d73de8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Evasive."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb7f24e0-b976-4486-b7f3-24d5da66a99e",
                                                "sense_id": "72dc7b95-6990-3481-a3ea-2841df1f760a",
                                                "text": "a shuffling excuse"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "df95c9d4-dede-40bf-9f4e-57a754e6973d",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e5eb72d-b19b-39f6-a887-85bdb2c5312b",
                        "source_sense_id": "b45acf04-10f7-3fc2-8533-e847aede9d61",
                        "target_lang_word": "shuffle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shuffle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "74e1b908-e89b-3da9-92c5-ddaa8ff0ea11",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of mixing cards or mah-jong tiles so as to randomize them."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6248fdb3-cb0f-4232-9cfa-927a6e19bc88",
                                                "sense_id": "74e1b908-e89b-3da9-92c5-ddaa8ff0ea11",
                                                "text": "He made a real mess of the last shuffle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cb8a6769-efb9-337b-86ca-aba13a6e0650",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of reordering anything, such as music tracks in a media player."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "092fd5bf-0850-381b-b999-4e74ca50b00f",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An instance of walking without lifting one's feet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eb7e31d-0e67-4382-8360-abc5dc2ab7fd",
                                                "sense_id": "092fd5bf-0850-381b-b999-4e74ca50b00f",
                                                "text": "The sad young girl left with a tired shuffle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d7542cce-ff7e-3ef2-9602-d5c7b1076403",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A rhythm commonly used in blues music, consisting of a series of triplet notes with the middle note missing, so that it sounds like a long note followed by a short note, and suggests a walker dragging one foot."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "26d4a521-d5b5-35ce-9007-a29907ce3b2f",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A dance move in which the foot is scuffed back and forth across the floor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a39510a9-929d-3cd4-a98a-737bbc0bd591",
                                        "entry_id": "e32cd119-a547-3d75-a3c1-a85dfd5531c6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A trick; an artifice; an evasion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a949858f-71d7-43c6-9e95-712da3a06308",
                                                "sense_id": "a39510a9-929d-3cd4-a98a-737bbc0bd591",
                                                "text": "The Gifts of Nature are beyond all the Shams and Shuffles in the World."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shuffle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac6892f4-3f0c-348b-b1be-08464cfca98f",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put in a random order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6ec86c4-6609-4829-8531-4868267e2174",
                                                "sense_id": "ac6892f4-3f0c-348b-b1be-08464cfca98f",
                                                "text": "Don't forget to shuffle the cards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b177e1c-96f7-4e78-ac1b-c9aad240ec5f",
                                                "sense_id": "ac6892f4-3f0c-348b-b1be-08464cfca98f",
                                                "text": "You shuffle, and I'll deal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a01ed06c-e22a-4736-abb5-0cf170f292c4",
                                                "sense_id": "ac6892f4-3f0c-348b-b1be-08464cfca98f",
                                                "text": "The data packets are shuffled before transmission."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c796e5c5-39d6-40ae-b33a-63a8896e0f9d",
                                                "sense_id": "ac6892f4-3f0c-348b-b1be-08464cfca98f",
                                                "text": "I'm going to shuffle all the songs in my playlist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f1e0fdf3-e9b3-3293-bf4e-2ddd7e0943ec",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To change; modify the order of something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3828381-ea58-49e9-92bc-79f0242eb1c8",
                                                "sense_id": "f1e0fdf3-e9b3-3293-bf4e-2ddd7e0943ec",
                                                "text": "But, rather than make a change up front, Hughes shuffled his defence for this match, replacing Carlos Salcido with Baird, in a move which few would have predicted would prove decisive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To move in a slovenly, dragging manner; to drag or scrape the feet in walking or dancing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4326881d-fec9-4c64-8175-50efc97ecce8",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                                "text": "He shuffled out of the room."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "70c9c66d-8b02-4fa7-b1c3-21ee653f8ae3",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                                "text": "I shuffled my feet in embarrassment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1135a887-844e-4b24-9e96-e7633618baf1",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                                "text": "[T]he aged creature came, / Shuffling along with ivory-headed wand, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f0dde87-5cf5-4da8-b9d3-a1609d73148c",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                                "text": "Even when the other instruments were resting the pianist kept up his monotonous vamping, with a dreary furbelow for embellishment here and there, to which some few of the dancers continued to shuffle round the floor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bd1131b-7ce4-46d4-a4a2-084ef2e2cf66",
                                                "sense_id": "e2d6b714-34d6-312a-82c1-32c53aa3dedb",
                                                "text": "The regular crowd shuffles in"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3cab6ced-8736-3a6d-99db-afd3f9eb8cf0",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To change one's position; to shift ground; to evade questions; to resort to equivocation; to prevaricate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "aa505446-f819-4987-8dcd-37f16d36f24f",
                                                "sense_id": "3cab6ced-8736-3a6d-99db-afd3f9eb8cf0",
                                                "text": "I myself, […] hiding mine honour in my necessity, am fain to shuffle."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60b28f77-1d95-3836-af4b-ee6def709b80",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To use arts or expedients; to make shift."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bff0c258-ebcb-4091-8662-321d8d358170",
                                                "sense_id": "60b28f77-1d95-3836-af4b-ee6def709b80",
                                                "text": "Your life, good master, / Must shuffle for itself."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c160cde-df59-3592-83d3-5d611d929dd4",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To shove one way and the other; to push from one to another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6462c69d-727e-40df-8399-b76305f6142b",
                                                "sense_id": "9c160cde-df59-3592-83d3-5d611d929dd4",
                                                "text": "to shuffle money from hand to hand"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a98234dc-6e0b-31b1-b21d-ea2a1920e97f",
                                        "entry_id": "c38777ea-b88a-3315-811a-ff80b36a8562",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To remove or introduce by artificial confusion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad9b9955-a2cc-4f8e-beb1-05ccafe29b79",
                                                "sense_id": "a98234dc-6e0b-31b1-b21d-ea2a1920e97f",
                                                "text": "Therefore you do vvell to have recourſe to your laſt Evaſion, that it vvas contriv'd by your Enemies, and ſhuffled into the Papers that vvere ſeiz'd: vvhich yet you ſee the Nation is not ſo eaſy to believe as your ovvn Fury; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3fcc4c9e-4067-4211-9f36-84f237713da6",
                        "source_entry_id": "1e5eb72d-b19b-39f6-a887-85bdb2c5312b",
                        "source_sense_id": "b45acf04-10f7-3fc2-8533-e847aede9d61",
                        "target_lang_word": "shamble",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "shamble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96ec8dec-cb51-344a-8696-53468fdcf7f8",
                                        "entry_id": "47b14b69-0e58-3ede-9231-09dad55549ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To walk while shuffling or dragging the feet."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db917adb-740c-4f41-8a03-f1e7dc814469",
                                                "sense_id": "96ec8dec-cb51-344a-8696-53468fdcf7f8",
                                                "text": "I wasn't too impressed with the fellow, when he shambled in unenthusiastically and an hour late."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "677d3e94-2e00-4b7e-b4e8-550c2c054976",
                                                "sense_id": "96ec8dec-cb51-344a-8696-53468fdcf7f8",
                                                "text": "The old black, not in any very high glee at having been previously roused from his warm hammock at a most unseasonable hour, came shambling along from his galley, for, like many old blacks, there was something the matter with his knee-pans, which he did not keep well scoured like his other pans; [...]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "shamble",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8ebbc8b1-a718-3f2d-bcb0-b4e6bd9010b1",
                                        "entry_id": "ccf69500-d83b-3f07-9dae-84aeb82dbb36",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One of a succession of niches or platforms, one above another, to hold ore which is thrown successively from platform to platform, and thus raised to a higher level."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
